{"text":"Mix: the water-cement ratio governs both strength and permeability. Lower w/c gives stronger, denser, more durable concrete. Never add water at site to recover lost workability - use an approved admixture instead.

Place: limit free fall height to about 1.5 m to avoid segregation, place in layers, and vibrate just enough to consolidate. Over-vibration drives coarse aggregate down and brings laitance to the surface.

Cure: start curing as soon as the surface can take it without damage, and keep it continuously moist for at least 14 days. Intermittent wetting and drying is worse than no curing at all for surface durability.","explanation":"IS 456 sets minimum cement content, maximum w/c ratio and minimum grade for each exposure condition. For severe exposure in reinforced concrete the minimum grade is M30 - that requirement exists for durability, not strength."}
